ISSUE 826

HTML entities can only have up to seven digits,
or six hexits.

```````````````````````````````` example
&#00000000; &#x0000000;
.
<p>&amp;#00000000; &amp;#x0000000;</p>
````````````````````````````````

&#5307530; is invalid unicode. As described in the spec,
invalid unicode is replaced with the unknown U+FFFD.

```````````````````````````````` example
&#5307530;
.
